#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:5
msgid "Best Practices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:7
msgid ""
"This guide provides recommendations and best practices for compiling C and C+"
"+ to the modern web using WebAssembly and Emscripten."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:10
msgid ""
"Following this guide when reporting bugs can also help speed up diagnosing "
"and fixing issues since you will be on the well-trodden path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:13
msgid ""
"In some cases, Emscripten will guide you towards these best practices by "
"emitting warnings, but that is not always possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:18
msgid "General Recommendations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:20
msgid ""
"**Avoid high-frequency calls between WebAssembly and JavaScript**; for "
"example, avoid per-pixel or per-sample calls in favor of operations that "
"process entire memory regions or buffers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:23
msgid ""
"**Avoid shipping debug information in production**; see below for "
"recommended release build flags."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:28
msgid "Command-Line Style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:30
msgid ""
"Keeping the command line flag usage minimal and consistent helps with "
"codebase understanding and avoids deviating from the well-lit path."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:33
msgid ""
"**Don't pass settings that are enabled by default.** To keep command lines "
"clean and concise, omit redundant options that are already default in modern "
"Emscripten (such as ``-sWASM=1``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:36
msgid ""
"**Prefer standard compiler flags** over Emscripten-specific ones where "
"possible (for example, prefer ``-pthread`` over ``-sUSE_PTHREADS`` and ``-"
"m64`` over ``-sMEMORY64``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:39
msgid ""
"**Use simple comma-separated lists** for list-based settings (for example, "
"``-sEXPORTED_FUNCTIONS=_main,_malloc`` rather than JSON arrays like ``-"
"sEXPORTED_FUNCTIONS=['_main','_malloc']``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:42
msgid ""
"**Avoid long lists on the command line**; use a response file "
"(``@filename``) instead (for example, ``-"
"sEXPORTED_FUNCTIONS=@exported_funcs.txt``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:44
msgid ""
"**Don't include the \"=1\" suffix for boolean flags.** For example, write ``-"
"sSTRICT`` and ``-sALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH`` rather than ``-sSTRICT=1`` or ``-"
"sALLOW_MEMORY_GROWTH=1``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:47
msgid ""
"**Use separate compilation** by compiling ``.cpp`` sources to ``.o`` object "
"files before linking rather than combining everything into a single "
"monolithic compiler invocation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:53
msgid "Recommended Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:55
msgid ""
"``-sSTRICT``: Opt into strict modern Emscripten behavior, disabling "
"deprecated or legacy compatibility features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:57
msgid ""
"``-sEXPORT_ES6``: Output a modern ES6 module (``module.mjs``). This option "
"implies ``-sMODULARIZE`` so the generated code will be encapsulated and not "
"impact the global namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:60
msgid ""
"``-sENVIRONMENT=web``: Limit the runtime support to only the environments "
"you are targeting. This reduces code size by, for example, omitting Node.js "
"and compatibility code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:63
msgid ""
"``-Werror -Wall``: Treat warnings as errors to catch C++ bugs and invalid "
"compiler settings early."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:65
msgid ""
"``-O3``, ``-Os``, or ``-Oz``: For release builds, choose ``-O3`` when "
"runtime performance is most critical, or ``-Os`` / ``-Oz`` when minimizing "
"binary payload size is the priority."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:68
msgid ""
"``-flto``: Enable Link-Time Optimization (LTO) during both the compilation "
"and linking steps of release builds for maximum runtime performance and size "
"reduction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:74
msgid "Debug vs. Release Profiles"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:76
msgid ""
"When configuring build profiles, keep compile and link flags consistent "
"within each configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:79
msgid ""
"**Release Builds:** Use ``-Oz``, ``-Os`` or ``-O3`` combined with ``-flto``. "
"Add ``--closure=1`` to get minified JavaScript too, unless you plan to "
"minify with an external tool."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:82
msgid ""
"**Debug Builds:** Use ``-g`` when compiling and either ``-g``, ``-gline-"
"tables-only``, or ``-gsource-map`` when linking. Avoid optimization flags "
"(such as ``-O2`` or ``-O3``) or ``-flto`` during debug builds for faster "
"compilation and accurate debugging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:89
msgid "Common Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:92
msgid "Asynchronous Code Execution and Main Thread Blocking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:94
msgid ""
"**Don't run long synchronous loops on the browser main thread.** The browser "
"uses cooperative multitasking; blocking the main UI thread prevents "
"rendering and freezes the web page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:98
msgid ""
"Restructure infinite loops to yield to the event loop "
"using :c:func:`emscripten_set_main_loop` (see :ref:`emscripten-runtime-"
"environment-howto-main-loop`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:101
msgid ""
"For synchronous-looking C++ code that must pause (or interact with "
"asynchronous JavaScript APIs such as ``fetch()`` or Web Promises) without "
"refactoring into callbacks, use :ref:`Asyncify <yielding_to_main_loop>` (``-"
"sASYNCIFY``) or JavaScript Promise Integration (``-sJSPI``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/docs/compiling/best_practices.rst:105
msgid ""
"Offload heavy compute or blocking operations to background workers "
"using :doc:`multithreading and pthreads <../porting/pthreads>` (``-"
"pthread``)."
msgstr ""
